  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Regular and Safe Migration of Pakistani Labour Migrants Towards Germany</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pakistan is a top labour-sending country, with over 1 million Pakistanis migrating annually, often to Gulf and European Union (EU) countries. Despite significant interest in economic opportunities abroad, many young Pakistani migrants face the risks associated with irregular migration. To support the Government of Pakistan&#x2019;s (GOP) efforts to promote safe and regular migration, IOM plans to contribute by engaging with communities and civil society organizations to raise awareness about the importance of safe and regular labour migration and to highlight the risks of irregular migration. Under the proposed project, IOM also aims to inform potential migrants, especially young men and women, about safe and regular migration pathways and the opportunities available for them to migrate to Germany and other selected EU Member States.</narrative>
  </description>
